  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1259 PM CDT Fri Jul 24 2026\n\nHeat Concerns:\n\nHeat and humidity build back into the area this weekend, with \nafternoon and evening heat indices around a 100 or more for most \nlocations both Saturday and Sunday. Confidence in higher heat \nindices for this weekend compared to last weekend is a higher as dew \npoints look to climb into the lower to mid 70s, which can feel very \noppressive. One limiting factor may be wildfire smoke, but for now \nthe expectations are that the smoke will be somewhat limited so the \neffect on temperatures will likely not be that great. Will have a \nheat advisory area wide for the weekend with some potential for \nadditional heat headlines next week. As confidence grows, a heat \nwarning may be needed along the James and Missouri River Valleys \nSaturday and Sunday where heat indices could climb to around 110. \nMost days next week look to have highs in the 90s, so even without \nheadlines will still be very warm each day.\n\nThunderstorm concerns:\n\nThe latest models continue to hint at isolated thunderstorm \npotential Saturday evening and early overnight. For now capping \nlooks to be a problem, but a weak wave is expected to move into \ncentral SD late afternoon so development may occur to the west of \nthe Mo River. As the wave shifts east isolated development will \nremain possible. Right now the main concerns look to be quarter \nsized hail and wind gusts to 65 mph.\n\nAnother piece of energy moves into the area on Sunday and should \nbring another chance for some isolated severe storms. The better \nshear and instability look to reside over southwest MN and this \nshould be the higher threat for severe storms. Will also need to \nkeep an eye out for south central SD where the cap could be broken \nand an isolated strong to severe storm could develop. Overall there \nmay be enough dry air in the low levels to really limit the \ninstability and them main concern would be wind if something could \ndevelop. Confidence for both Saturday and Sunday are fairly low.\n\nOther concerns:\n\nThe only other real concern will be the potential for some fog later \ntonight into Saturday morning. The better chances will be in \nnorthwest IA, northeast NE and far southeast SD. For now not looking \nlike widespread dense fog.",
